# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the sanitize CI job (.github/workflows/sanitize.yml).
#
# System libraries only. Every entry names a shared library that write-it
# links against, never a write-it function, file or test. Do not add an
# entry that matches write-it's own code (writeit::, src/, tests/, a
# write-it-* executable): a leak in write-it must fail the job.
#
# Each entry is here because a window suite aborts without it, from memory
# the library allocates and keeps for the life of the process:
#
#   libfontconfig  Pango's font map caches fontconfig patterns and font sets
#                  (pango_font_map_list_families -> FcFontSetList), first
#                  reached from MainWindow::fill_font_combo. Never freed.
#   libGLX_mesa    GDK probes GLX once in gtk_init (epoxy_glx_version).
#   libglib        GTK's file chooser, run by Save As in toolbar-overflow and
#                  import-clean: GFiles from its async enumeration, and the
#                  GError it drops for a cancelled GTask.
#   libdbus-1      With no session bus (CI's container has none), GTK's AT-SPI
#                  bridge fails to connect and libdbus keeps one DBusString
#                  (_dbus_string_lengthen). write-it never calls libdbus.
#
# How a match works: LSan suppresses a leak if any frame of its allocation
# stack matches. CI uses ASan's fast unwinder, which stops at the first
# library built without frame pointers, so a leak allocated by fontconfig or
# glib shows only that library's frame. So libglib also hides glib memory
# (g_strdup, g_malloc) that write-it itself fails to free. Memory write-it
# allocates with new or malloc is never hidden. To see every frame, run once
# with ASAN_OPTIONS=...:fast_unwind_on_malloc=0 (slow: minutes per suite).
leak:libfontconfig.so
leak:libGLX_mesa.so
leak:libglib-2.0.so
leak:libdbus-1.so
